<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eitel Friedrich II, Count of Hohenzollern</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1452–1512</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eitel Friedrich II (1452–1512) was Count of Hohenzollern and a close adviser and commander of Emperor Maximilian I, who made him the first judge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imperial-chamber-court">Imperial Chamber Court</a> in 1495 and hereditary chamberlain of the Empire. He restored the Swabian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hohenzollern">Hohenzollerns</a>' fortunes after the feuds of the 15th century, gaining the lordship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haigerloch">Haigerloch</a> in 1497 by exchange with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eitel-friedrich-ii-count-of-hohenzollern.jpg" alt="Eitel Friedrich II, Count of Hohenzollern" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:EitelFriedrichII.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
